  "id": "loanwolf",
  "neon": "#d8b45c",
  "note": "LOAN WOLF — a lender on the corner of the Gate Road, the last frontage out of the city and the\nfirst one back in.\n\nThe tile's prose: frosted glass to head height with the name in gold leaf across it, a heavy door,\nand rates on a card in the corner of the window in a type size that makes you stop and lean in.\nThe card is on the plinth under the window rather than on the glass, because a sign over glazing\nreads as two drawings on top of each other.\nThree floors.\n\nIt dresses as a bank and isn't one: a rusticated marble base with pilasters, a heavy bronze door in\na deep surround, two bays of frosted glass with the name gilded across them, and the rates card.\nThe two upper floors are regular windows between pilasters under a cornice, lit only on the first\nfloor where the desks are. Nothing here is lit after dark except the door lamp and the gilt.",
  "pal": "ty_marble",
